WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.280
Who else loves s’mores?

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:05.190
I’m gonna be honest, if it has s’mores
in the name, I am gonna try it, even though

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:08.710
I know FULL WELL it probably will taste nothing
like a s'more.

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:10.380
S'more ice cream? There.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:11.840
S'more M&amp;Ms? Got it.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.800
S'moreos? Sign me up.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.900
That’s why, when I see the Stay Puft Marshmallow
Man in Ghostbusters, all I want is the Giant

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.240
Hershey Bar Guy and the Oversized Graham Cracker
Lad to show up.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.700
That's when we’re having a party, my friends,
that's when!

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:40.980
[Film Theory Theme Plays]

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:45.739
Hello internet, welcome to Film Theory, the
show that asks questions about movies that

00:00:45.739 --> 00:00:49.570
others are too afraid to ask…or have too
much self-respect to ask.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.890
But I’ll let YOU decide which one it is!

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:56.890
Man, in a summer crammed full with movies,
there’s one that everyone is talking about:

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:00.780
Ghostbusters…but maybe not for the right
reasons.

00:01:00.789 --> 00:01:07.130
I mean the original 1984 version is an undisputed
classic, holding down a 97% fresh rating on

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:08.130
Rotten Tomatoes.

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.240
But then fast forward to today, where the
CGI-filled all-female reboot trailer is currently

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:17.600
the most disliked movie trailer in the history
of YouTube.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:25.179
Let me say that again: THE MOST DISLIKED trailer
in the HISTORY of YouTube.

00:01:25.179 --> 00:01:26.219
Really?

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:27.220
Really Internet?

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:30.400
THIS is so much worse than THIS?

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.140
"Are you going bald?"

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:37.060
"No, no, no, no, you're getting fatter, and your hair doesn't realize it needs to cover more face."

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:40.780
Hey I'm not judging, there is no accounting
for taste—and I understand, the comedic

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:44.220
stylings of Adam Sandler are truly transcendent.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:45.840
[Belches, then farts]

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:47.080
Comedy gold.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:51.660
So the goal for today: make a video that you like at least slightly better than the Ghostbusters trailer.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:55.000
Well, I'm already starting at an advantage,
because this video focuses on the original

00:01:55.009 --> 00:01:59.259
Ghostbusters, reminding you of that happier
era when watching a baby get repeatedly put

00:01:59.259 --> 00:02:03.600
into life-threatening situations was the epitome
of entertainment.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:09.940
Truly, when you think of the original movie
yeah, sure, you had crossing streams and the

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:15.940
demonic David Bowie, THE most iconic image is none other than the Stay Puft Marshmallow Man.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:19.540
It’s a moment so brilliantly absurd it became
an instant classic.

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:23.330
But while others were chortling away at Dan
Akyroid’s childhood memories of roasting

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:26.909
marshmallows by the fire at Camp Waconda here’s
where my theorist brain went to when I first

00:02:26.909 --> 00:02:28.920
saw the scene… could I EAT that?

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:33.380
And sure, maybe there’s some FatPat talking there, but hey, it’s all in the name of science.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:37.940
So, today I’m answering the question that’s
been on nobody’s mind since 1984: How many

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:41.190
calories are in the Stay Puft Marshmallow
Man, and what would it mean

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:43.060
if I were to actually eat him?

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:46.520
Now, for those of you who grew up not knowing
“who you gonna call” here’s the skinny

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:50.390
on our chubbiest of bunnies: In the original
Ghostbusters, the team takes on an ancient

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:53.290
Sumerian demon named Gozer who’s haunting
New York City.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:55.360
As you do, you know, the uzhe.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:59.150
As part of the final showdown, Gozer demands
that the heroes choose what will destroy them

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:00.340
and the rest of New York City.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:04.469
While everyone else tries to keep their minds
blank, our good buddy Dan Aykroyd accidentally

00:03:04.469 --> 00:03:08.939
imagines "I tried to think of the most harmless
thing,": The Stay Puft Marshmallow Man.

00:03:08.939 --> 00:03:12.300
And you can’t really blame him, because
images of Stay Puft are sprinkled throughout

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.300
the movie.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:16.599
When we see the eggs in Dana’s apartment
explode and cook on the counter, a bag of

00:03:16.599 --> 00:03:20.420
Stay Puft marshmallows are there on the counter
with the rest of the groceries, and later

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:24.530
in the film we see a big mural for Stay Puft
Marshmallows on the side of a building.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:27.569
With all those brand integrations, poor Ray
didn’t stand a chance.

00:03:27.569 --> 00:03:28.590
Subliminal advertising, guys!

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:32.299
You gotta put a #spon on those sorts of things,
sellouts.

00:03:32.299 --> 00:03:36.579
Anyway, the great big Mallow Blaster appears,
Godzilla-style, and starts pounding upper

00:03:36.579 --> 00:03:37.900
Manhattan into fluff.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:38.900
Hilarity ensues.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:43.079
So, let’s figure out just how much marshmallow
action the kaiju Puff is packing.

00:03:43.079 --> 00:03:46.760
To do this, we need to make some assumptions
about the Stay Puft Marshmallow Man’s contents.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:50.370
Let’s just say that he’s made entirely
of marshmallow; normally I’d say he’d

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:54.201
need some kind of musculo-skeletal system
to maneuver, but seriously, he’s a giant

00:03:54.201 --> 00:03:59.450
snack food manifested out of Dan Aykroyd’s
subconscious and compelled by a demon of hell,

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:02.359
so we’re going to let the normal anatomy
slide on this one.

00:04:02.359 --> 00:04:05.940
Plus, when he erupts, there ain’t no viscera,
just a bunch of marshmallow fluff, so I think

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:06.940
we’re safe.

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:10.590
Now, the first step in determining how much
of a caloric punch Stay Puft packs is determining

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:12.180
just how large he is.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:15.800
In the movie, they give us a hint: “Killed
by a 100-foot marshmallow man.”

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:17.680
But can we get more exact?

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.020
ABSOLUTELY!

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:24.190
In the DVD extras for Ghostbusters, Mark Stetson,
the model shop supervisor reveals that the

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:28.690
scaled size of the Stay Puft Marshmallow Man
was 112 and a half feet tall.

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:32.770
We can also compare that to the surrounding buildings to confirm that this is the right range.

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:36.620
So, for once, that made my life a bit easier,
but from there the calculations start to get

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:37.620
a bit trickier.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:40.780
Initially, I tried to determine the width
of the Stay Puft Marshmallow Man by looking

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.600
at his scale compared to other landmarks in
the movie.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:47.480
There’s a shot where the Ghostbusters are
looking down at Stay Puft as he walks towards

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:50.650
them, and we can see that he is about the
width from the sidewalk to the yellow center

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:51.950
lines on the street.

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:56.259
We know that this is about 50 feet, because
the street Stay Puft is walking on is Central

00:04:56.259 --> 00:04:57.889
Park West in New York.

00:04:57.889 --> 00:05:02.500
According to an 1892 edition of the World
Almanac, almost all avenues in New York City

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:05.580
are 100 feet wide, so Stay Puft is half that.

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:09.230
But we’re still missing depth and the movie
doesn’t really show many good shots from

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:10.230
the side.

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:13.930
And more importantly, even if we’re right
about Stay Puft being 50 feet wide at his

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:16.889
widest, how wide is his head compared to the
rest of his body?

00:05:16.889 --> 00:05:20.009
If you watch this series a lot, you’ll know
that I would usually account for this sort

00:05:20.009 --> 00:05:24.470
of thing using pixel measurements, but Stay
Puft is full of unusual shapes and sizes.

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:28.470
So in this case I'm using another measurement
that'll do a better job of taking Stay Puft

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:31.480
Marshmallow Man's irregular shape, and giving
us workable numbers.

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:33.819
And that measurement is BMI.

00:05:33.819 --> 00:05:37.870
The statistic of BMI was created in the 19th
century and is mostly used to measure the

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:42.970
relative thickness or thinness of a population by measuring average weight across average height.

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:46.760
And for our purposes, it’s actually perfect
because all it does is calculate a ratio of

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:48.850
height to width for a human-shaped object.

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:54.400
It doesn’t matter if the person is ripped, or overweight, or happens to be composed entirely of sugar.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:57.979
And looking at the Marshmallow Man, he’s
not just a bunch of cylindrical marshmallows

00:05:57.979 --> 00:06:00.830
stacked together—he’s got folds and girth
to them.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:03.550
He’s much more human than he is purely geometric.

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:07.740
So knowing that, take a look at this chart
of body shapes and their associated BMIs.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:10.790
Stay Puft is round and has relatively thick
limbs.

00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:14.310
From a purely scientific perspective, Stay
Puft’s shape indicates that he would have

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:15.960
a very high BMI.

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:21.610
And judging by the figures, a BMI of 40 is a good estimate, perhaps even a conservative one.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:24.900
Hey, we will have NO candy shaming on this
channel, okay?

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:28.110
But now that we have a height and a projected
BMI for the Stay Puft Marshmallow Man, we

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:30.080
can calculate how much he would weigh.

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:34.440
Or, more accurately, we can determine how
much a human being his size would weigh, and

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:35.440
then go from there.

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:40.560
The formula for Body Mass Index states that
BMI is equal to 703 times a person’s weight

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:43.889
in pounds divided by their height in inches
squared.

00:06:43.889 --> 00:06:48.650
Stay Puft’s height of 112.5 feet translates
to 1,350 inches.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:52.889
When we square the height, multiply the BMI
of 40 by that number, and then divide the

00:06:52.889 --> 00:06:59.220
result by 703, we have isolated weight, which
comes out to 103,698 pounds.

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:04.410
But now before you rage in the comments, no,
obviously he doesn’t weigh 103,000 pounds.

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:07.820
Like I said, that would be the weight of the
Stay Puft Man…Man.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:12.260
If the Stay Puft Marshmallow man were just
a—a human of Marshmallow Man size.

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:13.270
You get it.

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:15.180
What we’re looking for the MARSHMALLOW Man.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:18.419
So we need to convert his weight from this
figure—what he would weigh as a human—to

00:07:18.419 --> 00:07:19.990
what he would weigh as a marshmallow.

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:24.030
To do that, we need to know what the density
of a human and a marshmallow actually are.

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:28.000
The density of human being does vary, but
for heavier-set people it’s usually around

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.349
1.01 grams per milliliter.

00:07:30.349 --> 00:07:35.819
Now we can adjust that weight of 103,698 pounds
to its marshmallow equivalent by converting

00:07:35.819 --> 00:07:40.960
human density to the density of a marshmallow,
which is 0.21 grams per milliliter, about

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.550
a fifth the density of a human.

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:46.310
So, doing all the math, that means the Stay
Puft Marshmallow Man actually weighs in at

00:07:46.310 --> 00:07:52.060
21,561 pounds, or about 9,500 kilograms.

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:56.080
Which is actually surprisingly light for a
building-crushing monster.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:00.659
For perspective, that’s lighter than a typical
school bus, so having him destroying buildings,

00:08:00.659 --> 00:08:02.370
may be a bit of a stretch.

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.090
He’s still a giant marshmallow.

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:10.210
Even at such an enormous of a size, his squishy Stay Puft-ness would just puff off most well-made buildings.

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:14.300
But I hear you in the comments saying “Geez,
MatPat, I came here because I want to eat

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:17.650
an ancient Sumerian demon, and not talk about
school buses.”

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:21.930
And that’s valid, I totally understand your
desire to eat an ancient Sumerian demon.

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:24.889
So now that we know how much he weighs, figuring
out the number of calories he contains is

00:08:24.889 --> 00:08:25.889
really no sweat.

00:08:25.889 --> 00:08:29.819
For reference, I used the nutrition facts
of Kraft’s Jet Puffed marshmallows because

00:08:29.819 --> 00:08:33.770
something tells me they're not that different,
which claim to have 100 calories for every

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:37.650
four marshmallows, or 30 grams, 20 grams of
which is pure sugar.

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:41.600
When we convert the weight of Stay Puft in
pounds to grams and multiply that by the number

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:46.470
of calories per gram, we get our whopping
total: the Stay Puft Marshmallow Man comes

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:51.170
out to be 32.6 million calories.

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:55.610
Get ready to hit that Pilates class...a few
hundred thousand times.

00:08:55.610 --> 00:09:02.030
If you wanted to consume that many calories,
you’d have to down about 228,000 cans of

00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:10.400
Coca-Cola, or eat 2.7 million peanut M &amp; Ms, or have 62,700 Big Mac meals from the Golden Arches.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:15.780
Considering that the average human life is
27,375 days, you would practically have to

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:22.090
have the Big Mac meal three times a day, every
day, for the rest of your life to get to that

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:23.660
level of caloric intake.

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:25.880
Which in turn, begs the question:
What about burning it off?

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:30.880
Well, a good rule of thumb is that a typical
person will burn 100 calories per mile walking.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:36.590
So that would translate to you walking 326,000
miles to work off your Marshmallow Man binge.

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:39.860
And if that sounds like a lot, you don’t
know the half of it!

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:43.380
The circumference of the Earth is just about
25,000 miles.

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:50.381
So you’d have to walk around the ENTIRE
GLOBE 13 times to burn off that Sumerian Demon

00:09:50.381 --> 00:09:51.381
you consumed.

00:09:51.381 --> 00:09:53.900
Man, I knew I should have ordered off the
lighter menu.

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:56.500
That Caesar Salad Titan was calling my name.

00:09:56.500 --> 00:10:00.660
Considering the average caloric intake for
a man is about 2000 a day, that’s nearly

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:04.770
44 YEARS worth of calories in a single serving.

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:05.770
Hungry?

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:06.770
Why wait?

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:08.980
Eat a Marshmallow Man, you'll be set for life.

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:11.160
And TALK ABOUT your sugar rushes.

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:16.810
One 100 foot tall marshmallow man is the equivalent
of 6.52 millions grams of sugar.

00:10:16.810 --> 00:10:24.030
That’s 7 American tons of sugar, the equivalent
of an adult African elephant made entirely

00:10:24.030 --> 00:10:25.030
of sugar.

00:10:25.030 --> 00:10:29.820
It’s nearly 1.5 million Oreo cookies—single
stuffed, which let’s be honest, is clearly

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:33.670
inferior to Double Stuft, so it’s actually
1,000,000 Double Stuft Oreos.

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:37.530
You may have seen the studies about how much
humans have increased their sugar intake over

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:38.780
the course of our history.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:43.290
It’s estimated to have risen 600% over the
last 140 years.

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:49.770
We now consume 130 pounds or 60,000 grams of sugar each year, which admittedly is a lot.

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:55.740
But even with in the face of this huge increase
in sugar intake, Stay Puft represents 108

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:59.080
years of constantly shoving sugar into your
face.

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:03.340
So needless to say, the Stay Puft Marshmallow Man does not seem to be part of a balanced diet.

00:11:03.340 --> 00:11:06.780
But the big question of the day remains: could
you eat him?

00:11:06.780 --> 00:11:11.100
Technically, the answer is yes, but the fine
print would say “But not for very long.”

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:12.840
And the problem is with the sugar.

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:17.220
Toxicologists believe that the lethal dose
of sugar for a human being is about 15 grams

00:11:17.220 --> 00:11:18.550
per kilogram of weight.

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:22.180
I say believe because these are estimates;
apparently, it’s pretty hard to find test

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:25.650
subjects who are willing to eat sugar until
they die, go figure.

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:27.620
Sometimes it feels like I come close though!

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:29.970
Sorry, that’s FatPat talking again.

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:36.200
For a 150 pound adult, that lethal dose would
be between 2 and 2.5 pounds of sugar or about

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:39.890
1,000 grams, which, all things considered,
isn’t all that much.

00:11:39.890 --> 00:11:44.840
If you were committed to eating the beast,
he would kill you 6,500 times over before

00:11:44.840 --> 00:11:45.840
you were through.

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:50.360
Which means, in an ironic twist, the scariest
thing about Stay Puft isn’t his physical

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:53.930
force—remember, he’s punching with less
strength and density than a school bus—and

00:11:53.930 --> 00:11:57.790
it isn’t crossing the streams, it’s his
sugar content.

00:11:57.790 --> 00:12:02.700
Forget getting stepped on, he would literally
kill you before you gnawed his toe off.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:05.980
But hey, that's just a theory.

00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:09.420
A Film Theory, aaaaaand cut!

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:13.560
But before I sign off, do you want to win
$50,000?

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:17.450
How about winning up to $2,000 every day for
